A macro call naming a config path that declares no macro fails the run with the macro exit
code, echoing the offending value and the path it could not resolve, and writes nothing.

-- fixtures/xdg/booping/config.yaml --
core:
  macros:
    build: ["false"]
-- fixtures/cwd/plan.md --
---
title: Foo
---
# Body
-- cmd --
booping frontmatter-update plan.md x="{{ macro('core.macros.nope') }}"
-- exit --
2
-- stdout --
-- stderr --
error: value "{{ macro('core.macros.nope') }}": no macro declared at config path: core.macros.nope
-- expected/cwd/plan.md --
---
title: Foo
---
# Body
